VK: a pipeline without a logic op passes a valid "VkLogicOp", for drivers that read it anyway.

With "LogicOp::NONE", PipelineVK sets "logicOpEnable = VK_FALSE" and "logicOp" from
g_LogicOps[NONE], which is VK_LOGIC_OP_MAX_ENUM (0x7FFFFFFF). That is legal: "logicOp" must be a
valid VkLogicOp only when "logicOpEnable" is VK_TRUE
(VUID-VkPipelineColorBlendStateCreateInfo-logicOpEnable-00607), and the validation layer is silent.

Mesa's lavapipe converts it regardless: lvp_execute.c:1045 (Mesa 26.2.6, handle_graphics_pipeline)
calls vk_logic_op_to_pipe(ps->cb->logic_op) without looking at logic_op_enable, and that switch
(src/vulkan/runtime/vk_blend.c) ends in UNREACHABLE, which an MSVC build turns into __assume(0): the
jump table loses its range check and 0x7FFFFFFF jumps to a garbage address. Measured with
mesa-dist-win 26.2.6 and 25.2.8 on Windows (the symbolized stack ends at that line): 25 tests crash
the process with an access violation on lavapipe's queue thread, drawing with depth or stencil,
blending, multisampling, indirect draws, mesh shaders. Linux builds of the same code do not crash.

This is a workaround for a driver defect, not an NRI defect: "logicOp" is VK_LOGIC_OP_COPY when the
logic op is off, a value every driver ignores in that state. With it the whole Vulkan suite runs on
lavapipe for Windows, and NVIDIA and Linux lavapipe are unchanged. Drop it once the pinned Mesa
converts the logic op only when it is enabled.

diff --git a/Source/VK/PipelineVK.hpp b/Source/VK/PipelineVK.hpp
index 9be9cb4c..a0af88c6 100644
--- a/Source/VK/PipelineVK.hpp
+++ b/Source/VK/PipelineVK.hpp
@@ -286,7 +286,7 @@ Result PipelineVK::Create(const GraphicsPipelineDesc& graphicsPipelineDesc) {
 
     VkPipelineColorBlendStateCreateInfo colorBlendState = {VK_STRUCTURE_TYPE_PIPELINE_COLOR_BLEND_STATE_CREATE_INFO};
     colorBlendState.logicOpEnable = om.logicOp != LogicOp::NONE ? VK_TRUE : VK_FALSE;
-    colorBlendState.logicOp = GetLogicOp(om.logicOp);
+    colorBlendState.logicOp = om.logicOp != LogicOp::NONE ? GetLogicOp(om.logicOp) : VK_LOGIC_OP_COPY; // ignored with "logicOpEnable" off, but a valid value: lavapipe converts it anyway
     colorBlendState.attachmentCount = om.colorNum;
     colorBlendState.pAttachments = scratch;
 
